posts.body:
Hehe, I am glad you all like this plugin.
In the helper plugin I use a lot of synchronous file system calls. They work well in this case because you will see the loading spinner going until the processing is complete. For other preprocessing needs, which follow the same style as mine, they work well. Take for example this piece of code that did not make it into the final plugin:
JavaScript:
disablePlugin() {
            // Load
            const oldPlugins = this.fs.readFileSync(this.pluginsConfig, 'utf8');

            // Generate new text
            const before = '"Zeriab_MoarMapsHelper","status":true';
            const after = '"Zeriab_MoarMapsHelper","status":false';
            const newPlugins = oldPlugins.replace(before, after);

            // Backup copy (old backup is overwritten)
            this.fs.copyFileSync(this.pluginsConfig, 'js/plugins.js.backup');

            // Save updated data
            this.fs.writeFileSync(this.pluginsConfig, newPlugins, 'utf8');
        }
This does work as expected. Problem is that you need to close the editor without saving and open it again to see the change. If you don't close the editor but keep working in it then any saves will set the status of the script back to ON. So I chose not include this method.
You can also use this method for loading JSON objects. Just need to parse the json where I generate the new text and do your changes.
Please do not use the synchronous file system commands in plugins that should run during the actual game. Here you definitely should go with an asynchronous approach. If you want to load data files check out
DataManager.loadDataFile
. If you want to save and load data you create during a game then check out
StorageManager.saveZip
and
StorageManager.loadZip
. They are all located in
rmmz_managers.js
.
Sorry nio, but I believe devs should have the ability to shoot themselves in their own foot off if they so desire.
As for bigger maps. That is true. This plugin along cannot truly free the map makers. Only once we have a plugin for stitching maps together will we truly be free! (I don't plan on making such a plugin)
*hugs*

